ot/pull/122200.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122200.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nAdds unit tests for Math::snap_scalar_separation function, including 16 sign combinations of the four parameters. negative and positive p_step at snapped(), negative and positive p_target with symmetrical p_step and p_separation, p_step = 0 when pass into snapped(), p_step = 0 in snap_scalar_separation () itself with negative and positive p_target and some arbitrary floats parameters. The most important behavior I think is p_target can be snapped to a further number than the closest step its nearby. \r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAI disclosure: I designed and hand calculated all test cases myself; I use AI to help me understand how the function is use in the game engine and what separation is on the grid.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122200/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122200/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}